  </a>

<div class="author-name"><a href="/blog?author=54076dc2e4b035477def3a3c">Alexandra Caluen</a></div>
<p class="author-bio"><p>Alexandra is a dance-obsessed office worker who moved to California after graduate school and found a great community in Los Angeles.&nbsp; Not quite as great as the community described in The L.A. Stories, but definitely inspirational.&nbsp; Alexandra was instrumental in establishing the L.A. chapter of USA Dance, Inc (the governing body for amateur DanceSport in the U.S.) and has competed in American Rhythm and American Smooth styles at the local, regional, and National level, winning National medals in 2010.&nbsp; Among many highlights of LA life, Alexandra and her husband, along with several other USA Dance members, danced in the Rose Parade on New Year’s Day 2012. They now live in western North Carolina.</p>
<p>Favorite color: purple.&nbsp; Favorite wine grape: Zinfandel.&nbsp; Favorite music: all of it.&nbsp; Favorite movie musical: Singin’ in the Rain.</p></p>


